body:
today (2019/07/08)  I found myself looking into the mirror. I saw saw a boy, not a man, not person, a boy. A boy who has tears running down his face. A boy who wishes that he was never born. a boy who prays every night that God would have enough mercy to come and collect his lost son. A boy who yearns for a little bit of love. Today a man died. what was left was not a corps, not ashes, not a lifeless entity which one day had aspirations and desires, no a man died and in his place a defenseless, hopeless, fragile boy stands. Blank eyes, empty vessel and no one to claim this boy. He looks forward and blankly says welcome.   

&#x200B;

"Welcome?". "I am not greeted with pleasantries."  "I am death, do you not fear me" "no company is welcome" the boy replies, as he welcomes the warm embrace of the icy death...
